<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karnasuvarna</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karnasuvarna was the capital of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shashanka">Shashanka</a> of Gauda in the early 7th century, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murshidabad">Murshidabad</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bengal">West Bengal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Its site is identified with Rajbadidanga near Chiruti, where excavations uncovered a Buddhist monastery taken to be the Raktamrittika mahavihara described by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xuanzang">Xuanzang</a>. After Shashanka's death the city fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhaskaravarman">Bhaskaravarman</a> of Kamarupa.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karnasuvarna.jpg" alt="Karnasuvarna" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Czarhind · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karnasubarna_debaditya_chatterjee.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
